fp(47,5,main="The horse tries again and again to pull the load, and the carter whips him. The pain in his mind is as bad as the pain in his body. Then a lady steps up and asks the carter not to whip the horse any more.")
fp(48,17,main="On Ludgate Hill the horse falls from the heavy load and from tiredness. He thinks he will die. He hears a sad voice say it is all their fault. People loosen his harness and give him cordial.")
sub(49,3,"One weak old man liked me very much","One old man who walked in a shaky way liked me very much")
